# ANTI-REGRESSION POSITIVE — the narrowest control for the by-value
# `&`-projection write-through bug: a `&` of a WHOLE BARE LOCAL scalar.
#
# CORRECT TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend): prints 11.
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): also 11 — the lanes agree here.
#
# This is the only by-value shape that currently works, which is what pins the
# defect's boundary: it is not "`&` of an `int` is broken", it is "`&` of an
# `int` PLACE reached through any projection is broken" — see
# `sound_amp_byvalue_place_writethrough.gg`. A fix must move all nine rows there
# to 11 without disturbing this one.
#
# The seed is computed, not a literal, so the write cannot be const-folded away.
int seed():
    return 10

void bump_int(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    int loc = seed()
    bump_int(&loc)
    print(loc)
